    "created_at": "2018-03-22T20:17:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-22T20:17:48Z",
    "body": "Good point about the visible document thing. We don't really need that constraint.  It just creates an explicit path to a display device that can provide a vsync heartbeat.  But we don't need the connection to be that explicit.\r\n\r\nRegarding AudioContext, we want to avoid using APIs for thing that were not their original purpose because it can lead to all sort unintended weird bugs.  In this particular case, AudioContext is unable to apply GPU backpressure. This can cause the browser to hang if the app is pumping out rendering instructions faster than the GPU can process them. A purposely designed API on the other hand, can throttle down the frame rate when the GPU can't keep up, ensuring that the rendering backlog is never more than X frames behind.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/375443233/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
