    "updated_at": "2018-04-24T08:46:11Z",
    "body": "> an OffscreenCanvasContext.commit() function that blocks until the UA is ready to start receiving commands for the new frame. This enables busy-loop on worker type of applications.\r\n\r\nThis is very much unclear. Why do we want to block anything and possibly miss some frames if calculating a new frame after commit() returns takes too much time? ",
