    "body": "@smaug----, not sure if I get your question. We want to block because an application can generate frames much faster than the UA can consume, right? (either because of display sync, or because the UA is busy). This doesn't mean that the UA needs to block at all (it can triple or quad buffer), but that it CAN block if it's being overwhelmed by frames. \r\n\r\nThe way this was phrased was an attempt to capture a similar behavior to SwapBuffers on desktop graphics APIs.\r\n\r\n",
